From b13d3c0c1f6caeac5471fcdde783912bf1f23777 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 04:10:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add LICENSE.mecab-ko for the vendored native library

setup.py links _mecab against libmecab via mecab-config; CIBW_BEFORE_ALL_LINUX
builds that library from eunjeon/mecab-ko's own release tarball
(scripts/install_mecab_ko.py), and auditwheel then vendors the resulting
shared object into python_mecab_ko.libs/ inside the wheel (confirmed by
inspecting upstream's own published manylinux wheel, which ships the same
libmecab-*.so.2.0.0 with no license text for it at all).

mecab-ko's own COPYING offers a choice of GPL, LGPL, or BSD (see its GPL/LGPL/
BSD files) and carries no license text of its own beyond that -- it is a
Korean-dictionary fork of Taku Kudo/NTT's original MeCab, whose BSD text this
patch reproduces verbatim from mecab-ko's own BSD file. This is the same
resolution already used for the same tri-license on the mecab and
mecab-python3 ports in this repo. setuptools' license_files defaults
(LICEN[CS]E*/COPYING*/NOTICE*/AUTHORS*) pick this file up automatically
alongside the project's own LICENSE, with no setup.cfg/setup.py change.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [blocked: this port may only touch riseproject-dev/python-wheels]
---
 LICENSE.mecab-ko | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.mecab-ko

diff --git a/LICENSE.mecab-ko b/LICENSE.mecab-ko
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9ae6ded
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LICENSE.mecab-ko
